---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CheckMyCoach v2.2" description="Controlled offline evaluation on one fixed 40-case corpus">
  <div class="container-content py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="badge badge-gold">Engineering Prototype</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)]">v2.2</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)]">Verified: 2026-08-02</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="mb-4">CheckMyCoach</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-8">
        A four-module research prototype—route, assign rule-based tags, generate candidate revisions, and run deterministic surface checks—evaluated descriptively on one fixed 40-case constructed fitness-advice corpus.
      </p>

      <div class="card-static mb-6 border-l-4 border-[var(--color-primary)]">
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Final claim boundary</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed">
          These results describe one offline execution. They do not establish system superiority, validated detection, equivalence between baselines, deployment effectiveness, or human/user effects.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-static mb-6">
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">What the evaluation shows</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] list-disc list-inside">
          <li>CheckMyCoach implements a pipeline that routes selected cases and generates candidate revisions using historical UCS heuristics.</li>
          <li>Generic revision and Generic-plus-Oracle revision produced identical per-case decisions in this single execution; this is not an equivalence result and does not show that oracle information has no value.</li>
          <li>No delivered output passed every deterministic target-and-retention check; the evaluation is descriptive, single-execution, and not a validated effectiveness claim.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card-static mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-[1.1rem] mb-3">Pipeline trace</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] list-decimal list-inside">
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">M1 routing:</strong> 15 of the 40 constructed cases were routed to candidate generation under the historical heuristic.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">M3 candidate generation:</strong> every routed case returned a candidate revision from the generation model.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">M4 surface checks:</strong> 12 of 40 delivered outputs removed the predefined target feature; none passed every target-and-retention check.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">End to end:</strong> none of the delivered outputs passed every evaluation check.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="card-static mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-[1.1rem] mb-3">Baseline interpretation</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed">
          Generic and Generic+Oracle revision produced identical per-case decisions in this single execution. That observation is not an equivalence result and does not show that oracle information has no value.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="https://github.com/GBX-Max1220/CheckMyCoach" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">View code</a>
        <a href="/demo/checkmycoach/" class="btn">Pipeline demo</a>
        <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/" class="link-arrow self-center">← Back to trustworthy AI</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
